    <!-- PARALLEL STATE -->
    <div class="sec">
      <div class="sec-ey">Structure · Parallel State</div>
      <h2 class="sec-headline">A State Within a State</h2>
      <p class="sec-lead">Hezbollah is one of the most studied examples of a "parallel state" — an organization that exercises governmental functions (taxation, security, social services, courts) alongside, and often superior to, the formal government. In southern Lebanon and the Dahieh suburb of Beirut, Hezbollah has functioned as the primary governing authority for decades. The 2024 war damaged but did not eliminate this structure.</p>

      <div class="crisis-panel">
        <span class="cp-icon">🔴</span>
        <span class="cp-text">The 2024 Israel-Lebanon War (Sept–Nov 2024) resulted in significant damage to Hezbollah's military command, weapons caches, and tunnel infrastructure in southern Lebanon. Post-war reports indicate the organization is reorganizing toward decentralized cell structures. The parallel state social services network sustained less damage than military assets and remains partially operational.</span>
      </div>

